User reported "nn it is conflecting" after the Résidanat ladder shipped. Clarified
via options: the user picked "ladder looks broken/overlapping". This log records the
full diagnosis (which turned out NOT to be the ladder) and the fix.

## 1. Ruled out first

- Git: `git fetch` + `status --porcelain` clean; `main` == `origin/main` at `1822f79`
  (before fix); not ahead/behind. No merge conflict anywhere.
- Vercel deploy of the ladder: `residanat.ladderTitle` / FR / EN strings present in
  deployed bundles (`/_next/static/immutable/chunks/1tjjhrp3zc26l.js`,
  `3ufkdktyipktr.js`) — ladder code WAS live.
- CSS class audit: every class the ladder uses exists in the deployed compiled CSS
  (`283u0ey08x4_l.css`, 65,096 bytes). `grid-cols-3` present ⇒ the build scanned the
  component ⇒ its sibling utilities generated. Not a missing-token bug.

