## 4. ACTUAL CONFLICT: years list page (found during the same capture pass)

Evidence `ev_cc90c8861c6183f98b42794ee81b0ed616e311fba87a0946bf66817d12584a28`
(1280×5200, `/faculties/67e26ce8-28e8-453e-8f62-15befa263997/years`):

a) **False module counts.** Console showed 12+ "Failed to load resource … 500".
   The page fired 22 parallel `GET /years/:id/modules` calls (one per count badge);
   the Supabase pooler (~10-connection limit) 500'd some, and the card fell back to
   `?? 0` — a LYING count. Parsed DOM card table (before fix):

   - Résidanat [710e6f03 pharmacie] → "4 modules" (ok)
   - Résidanat [c046ca5b dentaire] → "7 modules" (ok)
   - Résidanat [e0af9889 medecine] → **"0 modules"** ← FALSE; the year holds 20
   - (all Internat/Year 1–6 rows read 0 — truthful, those years are empty)

b) **No track on cards.** Cards render `title={year.label}` only: "Internat" ×3,
   "Résidanat" ×3, "Year 1" ×3 … side by side, alphabetically sorted. Three
   identical "Résidanat" cards, one of them claiming 0 modules while its page
   inside shows 20 — this is the "conflicting" the user saw.

## 5. Fix (commit `a4acbe5`)

- Backend `src/routes/curriculum.routes.ts`: GET /api/faculties/:id/years now
  returns `moduleCount` per year from ONE grouped query
  (`prisma.module.groupBy({ by: ["yearId"], where: { year: { facultyId: id } } })`).
  Semantics match GET /years/:id/modules (modules by yearId alone; faculty
  visibility enforced above). One pooler connection replaces 22 parallel requests.
- Frontend `web/src/app/faculties/[id]/years/page.tsx` + `web/src/lib/types.ts`:
  uses the grouped count; only years lacking the field (old-backend deploy window)
  still batch-fetch; each card now renders its track label before the count
  (reuses i18n keys onboard.trackMed / trackDent / trackPharma).
- Gates: backend `npx tsc --noEmit` 0; frontend tsc 0; lint 0 errors (same 4
  pre-existing warnings); `next build` 0 (all routes).

