## Multi-module quiz builder + "repeat my last quiz" — same day, later
================================================================================

Feature: commit 0aa4d11 (7 files, specific paths) — backend: moduleIds[] accepted by
GET /api/questions/counts and threaded into the total + sittings queries (badges stay
single-module/year-scoped by design); GET /api/sessions/:id now echoes a derived
`config` {mode, size, timeLimitSeconds, resultSort, showStats, questionTypes, moduleIds,
unitIds} reconstructed from the questions actually SERVED (no schema change). Frontend:
module dropdown replaced by multi-select checkbox chips with live counts (same pattern
as units), units section gated to exactly one ticked module (disclosure otherwise),
"Répéter mon dernier quiz" prefill on /qcm/builder. Gates: backend tsc 0; web tsc 0,
lint 0 errors (4 pre-existing warnings in untouched files), next build exit 0.
Vercel + Railway deployed before live verification.

Disposable account verify-mmod-1028@example.com (id cb04cec7-986c-4893-bbd4-b5a76e04e7a8).
Password NOT recorded here (verification-discipline policy). Tokens below redacted.

### Backend, live on Railway (raw)

counts moduleIds discrimination (one authed GET per line):
- /questions/counts?moduleIds=3a5129d1-e4a4-46a0-8b17-a24419cc08f5  (alger Cardiologie)
  -> 200 {"total": 0}
- /questions/counts?moduleIds=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000030  (seed Cardiology)
